            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropy+groups"} isotropy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
              of the left action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
              are the two extreme cases
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Isotr
                        %mi ℍ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Isotr_{\mathbb{H}}(G) = \{1, G\} \in Sub(G)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivariantHomotopyOfSVInRODegreeV"}
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi G
                      %mo |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\vert W_G(1)\right\vert
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\vert G \right\vert
                    \\,.
            %p
              and all degrees must differ from that of the class of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
              by a multiple of this multiplicity. Finally, the offset of the identity function is clearly
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
